            {
                "entry_id": "deabe561-e08f-3344-96fc-1e46582e994d",
                "word": "ungood",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "18dc2eb6-7a12-301f-ab2c-3fe896da0863",
                        "entry_id": "deabe561-e08f-3344-96fc-1e46582e994d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Lack or absence of good; goodlessness; bad"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "rare",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8fb5d528-3199-484d-9ded-b7b5b7b31478",
                                "sense_id": "18dc2eb6-7a12-301f-ab2c-3fe896da0863",
                                "text": "Here we can see that electricity is merely a manifestation of the fundamental dichotomy of the dualistic universe, the struggle between Good and Ungood, between Yin and Yang."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "29c0d11c-4ea3-4ed3-9262-49ad6a62face",
                                "sense_id": "18dc2eb6-7a12-301f-ab2c-3fe896da0863",
                                "text": "This government has bought the myths and is determined to foist this 'ungood' on every Australian citizen. I say 'ungood' deliberately."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "007c5a11-71b0-4fdc-9115-7d4c7029df0a",
                                "sense_id": "18dc2eb6-7a12-301f-ab2c-3fe896da0863",
                                "text": "“[…] In some, however, the ungood has turned inside out. It tortures only the spirit within.”"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
